  "what": "Four fresh recovery signals, light recent load, nothing to change. `keep` is a decision and has to survive the same checks as any other.",
  "why-two-goals-out-of-order": "Deliberate, and not to be tidied. DH-1's second half asks whether the chain writes to the caller's own evidence, which it probes by freezing the context — and an in-place sort of a one-element array writes nothing, so a scenario with a single goal makes that probe silently inert. Two goals in the wrong order is the smallest input that makes an ordering mutation observable.",
